        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54bb77df-13e3-5003-bacf-568c7f3a3025",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Aberdeen Bestiary\n- Places: Palace of Westminster, River Thames, City of Westminster, London\n- Organizations: Aberdeen University Library, Old Royal Library, House of Commons, House of Lords, Parliament of the United Kingdom\n- Concepts: Scitalis, Medieval bestiaries\n\nFacts:\n- The Aberdeen Bestiary is a 12th-century English illuminated manuscript bestiary held as MS 24 at Aberdeen University Library.\n- The Aberdeen Bestiary was first listed in 1542 in the inventory of the Old Royal Library at the Palace of Westminster.\n- The Palace of Westminster is the meeting place of the House of Commons and the House of Lords, the two houses of the Parliament of the United Kingdom.\n- The Palace of Westminster stands on the north bank of the River Thames in the City of Westminster in central London.\n- The Palace of Westminster is commonly known as the Houses of Parliament.\n- The Scitalis, or Scytale, is a serpent in Medieval bestiaries, including the Aberdeen Bestiary.\n- The Scitalis is described as having marvelous back markings that stun viewers and slow them so it can catch them.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
